#!/bin/sh
# Data-leak guard (GRID license): blocks any push containing licensed data
# or derivatives. Installed by `make setup` (git config core.hooksPath .githooks).
# CI runs the same audit server-side; this hook is the first line of defense.

REMOTE="$1"
PATTERN='\.\(zst\|jsonl\|parquet\|sqlite\|sqlite3\|db\)$\|^\(val\|lol\|val-ability-supplements\|data\)/'

# Files about to be pushed (local ref vs remote), fall back to all tracked.
if command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    if git rev-parse --verify origin/main >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        FILES=$(git diff --name-only origin/main HEAD 2>/dev/null; git ls-files)
    else
        FILES=$(git ls-files)
    fi
else
    FILES=""
fi

BAD=$(echo "$FILES" | grep -E "$PATTERN" 2>/dev/null)

if [ -n "$BAD" ]; then
    echo "PUSH BLOCKED - licensed GRID data detected:" >&2
    echo "$BAD" >&2
    echo "The data license forbids committing data or derivatives (docs/COMPLIANCE.md)." >&2
    exit 1
fi

exit 0
